@start docs/webhooks.md
# Webhooks

Every webhook we send is signed. The signature is in the
`X-Order-Signature` header and is an HMAC of the raw body.

The payload is signed with the webhookSecret from the environment. Verify
it before you trust the body.

Delivery is retried with backoff. Retries stop after retryLimit attempts
and the event goes to `webhook_dead_letter`.

@expected docs/webhooks.md
# Webhooks

Every webhook we send is signed. The signature is in the
`X-Order-Signature` header and is an HMAC of the raw body.

The payload is signed with the `webhookSecret` from the environment. Verify
it before you trust the body.

Delivery is retried with backoff. Retries stop after `retryLimit` attempts
and the event goes to `webhook_dead_letter`.

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(protected orderRepository: OrderRepository) {}

  public async list(customerId: string) {
    return this.orderRepository.findMany({ where: { customerId } });
  }
}
